{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Dressing the Part", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "When an Interview Is a Nightmare", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future with Will, Going to and the Present Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are different ways to talk about the future - you can use the <span class=\"strong\">modal verb will</span>, the structure <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span> or the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous tense</span>. Each of these elements has its own use. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Refer to the chart for an outline of the use and the structure of each of these: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future or make predictions about the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ll </span>have to think of a good answer for that one for the future.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be Going To\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you talk about intentions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m going to</span> make sure I do a lot more research before my next interview.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">And I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m updating</span> the phone numbers of my references tonight!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I'm going to make sure I do a lot more research before my next interview. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll read everything I can find on the company website.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll think about answers to those tough questions!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm updating the phone numbers of my references tonight!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to talk about the future and you want to refer to an action that <span class=\"underline\">will be in progress at a certain time</span> in the future, you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous tense</span>. <br> You use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect tense </span> to talk about something that <span class=\"underline\">be complete by a certain time</span> in the future. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> structure: <br>will (not) + be + verb-ing <br>  For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Next week, I <span class=\"strong\">will be going</span> to an interview for a freelance journalist position.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> structure: <br> will + have + past participle<br>For example:  <br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will have been</span> to four different interviews in two weeks, but no luck so far. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Next week, I will be going to an interview for a freelance journalist position. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Tomorrow, I will be thinking of you doing your presentation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "On Friday, my sister will be applying for a job in the same company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will have been to four different interviews in two weeks, but no luck so far. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "By next week, we will have come up with a better name for the project.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "By the end of the month, the company will have hired 10 new employees.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be scheduled", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be planned to start at a certain time ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The interview was scheduled for 14:00, which in international time is 2:00 p.m. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about a bad interview experience.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ordeal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very difficult process", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What an ordeal. It was a nightmare interview!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "airline industry ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "business related to building and flying airplanes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The interview was for a job in marketing in the airline industry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "COO", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Chief Operating Officer, a high-ranking person responsible for the daily activities of a company", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  During the interview, the COO asked me a lot of unusual questions I wasn't prepared for.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mission statement", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a short description of a company's purpose and goals", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He also asked me what I thought about the company mission statement, which I didn't know.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Talk to 2-3 people about bad interview experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the reasons why they were bad experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online. Find more bad interview experiences to get ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the ideas to make up an original interview experience. Write 80-100 words describing what happened.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the words <span class=\"italic\">terrible</span>, <span class=\"italic\">nightmare</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ordeal</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your text to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about interview experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read about other interview experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a text describing a negative interview experience using appropriate vocabulary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my text with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can discuss future plans.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"